      ],
      "nets": [
        "/Microcontroller/NET0007",
        "Net-(J9-Pin_2)"
      ],
      "observed": "The TPS1H200AQDGNRQ1 output pin (U5 pin 7) is connected to screw terminal J9 pin 2. The specified heater screw terminal J6 pin 2 is instead connected to /Microcontroller/NET0007, the same net as ESP32 GPIO1 and the high-side switch IN/DIAG_EN pins.",
      "expected": "The specification states that the high-side switch OUT pin feeds the heater connector J6 pin 2. The user-accessible heater terminal should be on the switched 12 V output net, not on the 3.3 V GPIO/control net.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "OUT (pin 7) feeds the heater connector `J6` pin 2"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"5\") (name \"/Microcontroller/NET0007\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"J6\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"Pin_2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"IN\") (pintype \"input\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"25\") (name \"Net-(J9-Pin_2)\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"J9\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"Pin_2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"7\") (pinfunction \"OUT\") (pintype \"output\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "A heater connected to the intended J6 terminal would be driven directly by the 3.3 V MCU GPIO rather than by the 12 V smart high-side switch; the switched output appears only on the undocumented J9 terminal. This can make the heater fail to operate and can overload or damage GPIO1.",
      "confidence": 0.8
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist shows a miswired heater output: the TPS1H200 switch output is not connected to the specified J6 screw terminal, and J6 is tied to the GPIO/control net. This is a functional deviation from the intended design."
}

